# live run at 40x100 (round 2: the Jev panel is a one-row strip by default, TUI-DESIGN-2 §4.6, so the dynamic region is
# rule + live 2 + console 5 ≈ 8 rows, no longer the 15-row pinned pane), shrunk to 12x60 twice — once after a quiet
# 0.3 s, once right after a keystroke (a paint pending in Ink's throttle, the race the pty storm scenario hits) — and
# grown back in between: each shrink segment costs at most one clearTerminal (§18, research 20 §1; 0 when the frame
# already fits the 12-row terminal), the grow none; Ctrl-C aborts the run and the session exits 0 through /exit
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 0.3
send make the tests pass
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect step \d+/\d+
expect jev s\d+ · \d+ decisions
send steer draft
expect (?:›|>) (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*steer draft
sleep 0.3
resize 12 60
sleep 0.8
mark shrunk-quiet
resize 40 100
sleep 0.8
mark grown
send Z
resize 12 60
sleep 0.8
mark shrunk-after-key
resize 40 100
sleep 0.8
mark grown-again
send \x03
expect Type to steer
send \x03
expect finished [·-] human_abort
expect Follow-up, question
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
